  "description": "The Backroad Apex AXS XPLR is an unconditional guarantee of fun and your entry into the world of electronic shifting. Shift gears faster, lighter and more reliably than ever before – without a front derailleur and without dropping the chain. The sophisticated gradation of the Apex 12-speed cassette provides the right gear for almost every situation. Your interface to the ground are the lightweight and robust ROSE G-THIRTY LIGHT gravel wheels made of aluminium, fitted with wide, grippy gravel tyres from WTB that generate a lot of safety and comfort. Speaking of comfort: You will love the wide Ritchey gravel handlebar not only for its good controllability, but also for its ergonomic qualities. A harmonious overall package that, at just 8.8 kg, sets you no limits from sporty to fun. More long distance | Endurance Flex is fun: The deep cut-out in the seat tube provides a massive increase in comfort, while the balanced frame geometry offers perfect handling on the road, gravel and technical terrain. Only a dry throat can stop you. More off-road | Action The frame and fork allow for a tyre width of up to 45 mm with 700c and up to 47 mm with 650b wheels. For rougher road conditions, perfectly adapted protectors at the down tube and chainstays protect the paint. More experience | Adventure Thanks to its many attachment points for bottle cages, Anything Cages or bags, the Backroad offers ultimate versatility, perfect for a day trip or bikepacking adventures. ¹ Weight: approx. 8.8 kg may vary by up to +/- 5% due to manufacturing tolerances. Weight with frame colour dusty purple, size 57 cm, without pedals. *Slight colour and paint deviations possible on frame and fork set.",
